-- title:
--   Finite type of the two integral chart algebras over ℤ
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and let $F = \mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,N$ be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set of $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,d\,j_q$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid N$; let $j = \mathtt{jFull}\,N \in F$ be the element of $F$ given by the $q$-expansion $j_q$ itself. For a set $S \subseteq F$, the chart algebra $\mathtt{chartAlg}\,\mathbb{Z}\,F\,S$ is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those $x \in F$ that are integral over the subring $\mathbb{Z}[S]$ generated by $S$, i.e. the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}[S]$ in $F$; here $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}$ takes $S = \{j\}$ and $\mathtt{chartAlgInf}$ takes $S = \{j^{-1}\}$. The assertion is the conjunction of two statements: the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}[j]$ in $F$ is a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra, and so is the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}[j^{-1}]$ in $F$.
--
--   These two rings are the affine charts of the two-chart integral model over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ attached to the modular function field of level $N$ and the coordinate $j$, the classical normalisation of the $j$-line; their finite generation over $\mathbb{Z}$ is what makes the glued scheme a model of finite type. The result is used downstream in the construction and analysis of the integral models of modular curves, notably in establishing integrality and local Noetherianity of the level structures and in comparing chart algebras under the constructed isomorphisms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_finiteType_int_chartAlgFin_and_chartAlgInf.lean

